concept control_flow {
  name     = "Control Flow"
  summary  = "if/else, match with patterns, if let, let bindings, blocks, and try/catch."
  related  = [if_else, match_expr, if_let, let_bindings, block_expressions, try_catch, patterns, expressions]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "WCL's expression-level constructs combine to compute values from values. Every construct here is an **expression**: it returns a value, never a statement."
    p "- [if / else](concept_if_else) — multi-way branches that agree on a type."
    p "- [match](concept_match_expr) — test a value against a sequence of patterns, with guards."
    p "- [if let](concept_if_let) — bind and branch on a single pattern in one step."
    p "- [let bindings](concept_let_bindings) — name a reusable value or function."
    p "- [Block Expressions](concept_block_expressions) — `let` bindings followed by a tail expression."
    p "- [try / catch](concept_try_catch) — recover from any evaluation failure."
    p "- [Patterns](fact_patterns) — the full pattern syntax used by `match` and `if let`."
  }
}
